--&gt;</description></item><item><title>II.i.2 (House of Aemilius Primio and Aemiluis Saturninus)</title><link>https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/id/9a0462febf/</link><pubDate>Wed, 21 Apr 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/id/9a0462febf/</guid><description>&lt;!-- ## Dates --&gt;
&lt;h2 id="excavation-dates"&gt;Excavation Dates&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1915, 1985&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="house"&gt;House&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;House of Aemilius Primio and Aemiluis Saturninus&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="garden"&gt;Garden&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Small garden to the rear of a &lt;a href="http://vocab.getty.edu/page/aat/300005366" target="_blank"&gt;taberna&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Behind the shop, living quarters were located, including a garden to the rear. The west garden wall was topped with the broken &lt;a href="http://vocab.getty.edu/page/aat/300148696" target="_blank"&gt;amphorae&lt;/a&gt;]; this wall was shared with the rear open area in I.i.1.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="bibliography"&gt;Bibliography&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;W. F. Jashemski, 1993, &lt;em&gt;Gardens of Pompeii: Herculaneum and the villas destroyed by Vesuvius. Volume 2, Appendices, p.75.&lt;/em&gt; &lt;a href="https://search.worldcat.org/title/222353569" target="_blank"&gt;(worldcat)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="keywords"&gt;Keywords&lt;/h2&gt;
